<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 17 June, from 653 to 1994.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">653 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,373 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Martin I is arrested for opposing Monothelitism</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pope Martin I, an opponent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monothelitism">Monothelitism</a>, was arrested in the Lateran in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> with Maximus the Confessor on the orders of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constans-ii">Constans II</a> and taken to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. He was later banished to Cherson, where he died.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monothelitism">Monothelitism</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caliphate.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/656">656 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,370 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Caliph Uthman is assassinated in Medina</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rebels besieging the house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uthman-ibn-affan">Uthman ibn Affan</a>, the third <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, who had refused their demand for a new caliph, set it on fire, broke in and killed him. His murder triggered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-fitna">First Fitna</a>, a civil war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assassination-of-uthman">Assassination of Uthman</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uthman-ibn-affan">Uthman ibn Affan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1462">1462 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">564 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Vlad the Impaler attacks the Ottoman camp by night</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Vlad III of Wallachia led a night raid on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a>'s camp near Târgovişte, failing to kill the sultan. His reputation for cruelty later fed the legend behind Bram Stoker's Dracula.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1579">1579 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">447 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Francis Drake claims Nova Albion for Elizabeth I</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During his circumnavigation, Drake landed on the coast of what is now northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> and claimed it for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> as Nova Albion. England made no attempt to settle it.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1775">1775 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British take Breed's Hill at heavy cost in the Battle of Bunker Hill</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After two failed assaults, British troops drove colonial militia from the heights near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a>. They suffered more than 1,000 casualties, proving the Americans could stand against regulars.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Iceland becomes a republic</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thingvellir">Þingvellir</a>, the site of its ancient assembly, Iceland ended its union with the Danish crown and proclaimed a republic. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> was then under German occupation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1972">1972 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">54 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Five men are arrested in the Watergate building</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Burglars linked to President Nixon's re-election committee were caught inside the Democratic National Committee offices in Washington. The cover-up led to Nixon's resignation in 1974.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1994">1994 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">32 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">O. J. Simpson leads police on a televised chase</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">About 95 million viewers watched police follow a white Ford Bronco carrying the former football star along <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/los-angeles">Los Angeles</a> freeways. Simpson was later acquitted of murdering his ex-wife and her friend.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 17 June <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edward-i-of-england"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edward-i-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edward I of England</span><span class="tp">1239–1307</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jon-sigurdsson"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jon-sigurdsson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jón Sigurðsson</span><span class="tp">1811–1879</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/adolphus-frederick-vi-grand-duke-of-mecklenburg-strelitz"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Adolphus Frederick VI, Grand Duke of Mecklenburg-Strelitz</span><span class="tp">1882–1918</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 17 June <span class="n">10</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sakanoue-no-tamuramaro"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sakanoue-no-tamuramaro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sakanoue no Tamuramaro</span><span class="tp">758–811</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-i-the-brave"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/boleslaw-i-the-brave.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bolesław I the Brave</span><span class="tp">967–1025</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-i-albert"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-i-albert.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John I Albert</span><span class="tp">1459–1501</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-yoshiteru"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ashikaga-yoshiteru.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ashikaga Yoshiteru</span><span class="tp">1536–1565</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/injo-of-joseon"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Injo of Joseon</span><span class="tp">1595–1649</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/martin-miguel-de-guemes"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/martin-miguel-de-guemes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Martín Miguel de Güemes</span><span class="tp">1785–1821</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lord-william-bentinck"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lord-william-bentinck.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lord William Bentinck</span><span class="tp">1774–1839</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/nikolai-bobrikov"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/nikolai-bobrikov.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Nikolai Bobrikov</span><span class="tp">1839–1904</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mohamed-morsi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mohamed-morsi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mohamed Morsi</span><span class="tp">1951–2019</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/kenneth-kaunda"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kenneth-kaunda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Kenneth Kaunda</span><span class="tp">1924–2021</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
